      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.06,
          "end": 3.03,
          "en": "-: So let's understand the history of Git.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.03,
          "end": 4.5,
          "en": "Now it is interesting, that's why we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.5,
          "end": 5.97,
          "en": "this special video for it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 5.97,
          "end": 8.88,
          "en": "The thing is, if we talk about any open source project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 8.88,
          "end": 11.01,
          "en": "so what happens in open source project is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.01,
          "end": 13.53,
          "en": "we have multiple people working on the same project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 13.53,
          "end": 15.48,
          "en": "But you will say, hey, that also happens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 15.48,
          "end": 16.92,
          "en": "with normal projects, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 16.92,
          "end": 18.21,
          "en": "The thing is, in normal projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 18.21,
          "end": 19.38,
          "en": "we have limited set of people.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 19.38,
          "end": 21.12,
          "en": "Let's say if you are working for a company",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 21.12,
          "end": 23.76,
          "en": "and you are building a project, you have,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 23.76,
          "end": 25.86,
          "en": "let's say a set of people in a team,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 25.86,
          "end": 27.12,
          "en": "they will be working on it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 27.12,
          "end": 28.41,
          "en": "and then you trust everyone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 28.41,
          "end": 30.24,
          "en": "because they're a part of a project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 30.24,
          "end": 32.97,
          "en": "In the open source project, anyone can contribute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 32.97,
          "end": 34.62,
          "en": "Let's say one day I decided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 34.62,
          "end": 36.72,
          "en": "to be a part of one open source project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 36.72,
          "end": 38.16,
          "en": "Of course, it'll take some time for me",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 38.16,
          "end": 40.41,
          "en": "to understand the project and then if I feel,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 40.41,
          "end": 42.24,
          "en": "hey, you know, everything is good",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 42.24,
          "end": 43.2,
          "en": "in this particular project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 43.2,
          "end": 44.37,
          "en": "so let's say it's any OS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 44.37,
          "end": 46.38,
          "en": "Let's say we have this own TELUSKO OS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 46.38,
          "end": 49.47,
          "en": "and then one day I want to contribute to that particular OS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 49.47,
          "end": 51,
          "en": "I want to add a new feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 51,
          "end": 53.01,
          "en": "of let's say a blue connectivity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 53.01,
          "end": 54.39,
          "en": "Just for an example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 54.39,
          "end": 56.1,
          "en": "I can write my own module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 56.1,
          "end": 59.16,
          "en": "and add that in the OS in my machine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 59.16,
          "end": 61.56,
          "en": "but if I want the entire world to use it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 61.56,
          "end": 64.8,
          "en": "I have to send them the new code, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 64.8,
          "end": 66.6,
          "en": "But then how this thing will work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 66.6,
          "end": 68.19,
          "en": "how multiple people in the world",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 68.19,
          "end": 70.17,
          "en": "can contribute to one project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 70.17,
          "end": 72.48,
          "en": "In the earlier days, we used to do something called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 72.48,
          "end": 75.66,
          "en": "archive files or sending the patches, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 75.66,
          "end": 77.73,
          "en": "Now there's the same thing happened with Linux as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 77.73,
          "end": 79.86,
          "en": "Now if you know Linux kernel, very famous one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 79.86,
          "end": 81.66,
          "en": "The founder is Linus Torvalds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 81.66,
          "end": 84.36,
          "en": "and he's very particular about how Linux should work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 84.36,
          "end": 86.16,
          "en": "What are the features we should have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 86.16,
          "end": 90.84,
          "en": "Now, initial days when 1991 to 2002, it was more about,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 90.84,
          "end": 93.75,
          "en": "if you want to provide the features, you can send patches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 93.75,
          "end": 95.78999999999999,
          "en": "or you can use archive files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 95.78999999999999,
          "end": 97.89,
          "en": "But then in 2002 they started using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 97.89,
          "end": 100.25999999999999,
          "en": "some proprietary tool called Bitkeeper.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 100.25999999999999,
          "end": 102.45,
          "en": "Now Bitkeeper, I think, was free at that point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 102.45,
          "end": 104.61,
          "en": "and then they started using Bitkeeper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 104.61,
          "end": 106.77000000000001,
          "en": "so that they can get the contribution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 106.77000000000001,
          "end": 108.969,
          "en": "from the world easily now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 108.969,
          "end": 110.78999999999999,
          "en": "They don't have to go through",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 110.78999999999999,
          "end": 112.47,
          "en": "a manual process of doing that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 112.47,
          "end": 113.97,
          "en": "So they can simply use Bitkeeper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 113.97,
          "end": 115.68,
          "en": "and they can send their code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 115.68,
          "end": 117.3,
          "en": "and then they can do the merging as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 117.3,
          "end": 119.94,
          "en": "Now, the problem is at one point the policy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 119.94,
          "end": 123.15,
          "en": "of Bitkeeper changed and they started charging.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 123.15,
          "end": 125.43,
          "en": "Now the Linux community was doing it for free",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 125.43,
          "end": 128.25,
          "en": "and then the entire world was using Linux for free.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 128.25,
          "end": 130.05,
          "en": "So they thought it's a good time now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 130.05,
          "end": 131.97,
          "en": "to move away from Bitkeeper,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 131.97,
          "end": 135.21,
          "en": "and that's where Git was formed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 135.21,
          "end": 136.71,
          "en": "Of course, they tried to make it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 136.71,
          "end": 138.24,
          "en": "very different from Bitkeeper.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 138.24,
          "end": 140.34,
          "en": "So Bitkeeper was working a different way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 140.34,
          "end": 142.38,
          "en": "and Git worked in a different way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 142.38,
          "end": 143.55,
          "en": "Again, what is that different way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 143.55,
          "end": 147.48,
          "en": "that we understand once we start the actual implementation?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 147.48,
          "end": 150.72,
          "en": "But that's how, in 2005, Git started.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 150.72,
          "end": 152.46,
          "en": "It's not like someone thought, hey,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 152.46,
          "end": 154.11,
          "en": "let's do this version control system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 154.11,
          "end": 155.61,
          "en": "No, they were using something else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 155.61,
          "end": 158.97,
          "en": "It's just that because of some issue between the Bitkeeper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 158.97,
          "end": 161.43,
          "en": "and the community, they moved away from it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 161.43,
          "end": 163.07999999999998,
          "en": "and they started using Git.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 163.07999999999998,
          "end": 165.93,
          "en": "As I mentioned before, GIT is different from all different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 165.93,
          "end": 167.43,
          "en": "version control system, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 167.43,
          "end": 168.87,
          "en": "Even different from BitkKeeper.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 168.87,
          "end": 170.04,
          "en": "And since it is different,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 170.04,
          "end": 172.29,
          "en": "it has given some amazing features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 172.29,
          "end": 174.96,
          "en": "It is very simple to use, it is fast.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 174.96,
          "end": 177.15,
          "en": "It also allows you something called branching.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 177.15,
          "end": 180.45,
          "en": "Again, once we move towards the advanced part of Git,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 180.45,
          "end": 181.89,
          "en": "we'll understand what branching means.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 181.89,
          "end": 184.35,
          "en": "And it's a fun concept to learn and also to implement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 184.35,
          "end": 188.94,
          "en": "and it is fully distributed, which makes Git very famous.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 188.94,
          "end": 191.16,
          "en": "And I know we have done enough built up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 191.16,
          "end": 193.32,
          "en": "And the question is how do we use Git?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 193.32,
          "end": 194.61,
          "en": "We want to collaborate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 194.61,
          "end": 196.89,
          "en": "and we want to work with Git so that we can collaborate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 196.89,
          "end": 199.77,
          "en": "with different people and we can build a project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 199.77,
          "end": 202.02,
          "en": "It doesn't matter, is it for a proprietary project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 202.02,
